Windows CI: rustkit-js tests::a_deep_setter_chain_and_call_fit_the_default_recursion_limit fails on
the hosted runner with "RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded". The test runs 400 setter links
on an 8 MB thread but never sets the thread's native stack budget, so the turn gets Boa's 1 MiB
default; a non-incremental debug build (CI sets CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0) has larger frames and 400 links
do not fit. Reproduced locally with CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0. The test now gives its thread the budget
spawn_script_thread gives a script thread (half its stack). Upstream should take the same fix.

Remove when upstream takes it.

diff --git a/crates/rustkit-js/src/lib.rs b/crates/rustkit-js/src/lib.rs
index 8b289815..e15dfd0d 100644
--- a/crates/rustkit-js/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/rustkit-js/src/lib.rs
@@ -3592,6 +3592,10 @@ mod tests {
             .name("setter-depth".into())
             .stack_size(8 * 1024 * 1024)
             .spawn(|| {
+                // The budget a script thread gives itself (half its stack, as
+                // `spawn_script_thread`): without it the turn gets Boa's 1 MiB, which 400
+                // links overflow in a non-incremental debug build (CI).
+                set_thread_native_stack_budget(Some(4 * 1024 * 1024));
